{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015XkZsWF2b4HP8Ecd5oWwib","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Task Contract\n2\t\n3\t- Task: optimize official FlashInfer task `gqa_ragged_prefill_causal_h32_kv8_d128` on NVIDIA A800 (`sm_80`).\n4\t- Read `task/definition.json` for the exact signature, reference implementation, dtypes, shapes, and tolerances.\n5\t- Submission: `solution/solution.py` exposing the required `run(...)` entry point.\n6\t- Primary implementation must use Triton. PyTorch is allowed only for tensor metadata and launch plumbing.\n7\t- No Torch computational fallback, CPU/NumPy fallback, CUDA-extension fallback, or alternate implementation fallback.\n8\t- Feedback evaluation uses the fixed five official workloads in `task/feedback_workloads.jsonl`.\n9\t- One immutable kernel version over all five feedback workloads counts as one candidate evaluation.\n10\t- Candidate budget: 100 evaluations. Token soft limit: 1,000,000; normal completion limit: 1,500,000; absolute limit: 1,650,000.\n11\t- Token budget includes uncached input, cache creation input, cache-read input, and output tokens.\n12\t- Final evaluation: one full 21-workload evaluation for the best valid candidate, only after operator approval.\n13\t- Primary ranking metric: geometric mean speedup; every selected workload must pass correctness.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5c0f4e8-c04f-4834-a82d-b52a81e3bbaa","uuid":"ec8b3b3e-409c-4830-8156-54162ef39a1a","timestamp":"2026-09-16T16:49:31.358Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--flashinfer--gqa_ragged_prefill_causal_h32_kv8_d128/TASK.md","content":"# Task Contract\n\n- Task: optimize official FlashInfer task `gqa_ragged_prefill_causal_h32_kv8_d128` on NVIDIA A800 (`sm_80`).\n- Read `task/definition.json` for the exact signature, reference implementation, dtypes, shapes, and tolerances.\n- Submission: `solution/solution.py